Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: keyboard check on Welcome, keyboard steps only when
 needed
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Setup design (sable-setup-wizard-titan2, "Welcome + keyboard
verification"): Welcome names the phone and checks the physical
keyboard before Language, so Wi-Fi is step 3 of 8.

Welcome now shows, under "Welcome to SableOS": the device line
(sable_welcome_device, "First boot" here; SableSetupWizardOverlay says
"Zinwa Q25 first boot"), a card "Check physical keyboard · Type A 7 @
then press Enter" with one field, a Software keyboard link (physical
keyboard settings with Use on-screen keyboard, else input methods;
shown only when the screen exists) beside Accessibility, and the line
"Tab/arrows focus · Enter select · Back previous". Emergency and Start
are unchanged in the button bar.

The field takes focus when Welcome opens, so the first key types into
it. Start, and Enter in the field (0401's last-field rule), check it
with the pure sable/SableQuickCheck: "A 7 @" (spaces ignored, either
case) says "Keyboard works." and continues; an empty field continues;
anything else says it did not match (7 is Alt+Z) and stays, with the
field cleared. Nothing typed is kept; the field is not saved,
autofilled, suggested or learned.

The keyboard steps stay in the owner script but only show when needed:
the readiness step (0402) only when there is something to fix
(SableKeyboardState.showStep: not when Sable Keyboard is selected or
not in the build), and the full keyboard test (0404) only when the
Welcome check did not pass, as the recovery path with its on-screen
keyboard and Accessibility links. Both still count as step 2.

